    "incident_id": "gmail-shape-047",
    "outcome": "probable_cause",
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "description": "Most likely cause: observed Gmail attachment-send failures in cedar were rejected locally because the attachment argument was a signed URL string instead of the required uploaded file object, so requests failed before any Google/provider call.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_1a9957dc86e7",
          "ev_74f478a0842b",
          "ev_603d36f62204",
          "ev_42cd001d24f1",
          "ev_a68b18a4b624"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [],
        "confidence": "high",
        "assumptions": [
          "Conclusion is scoped to observed Gmail attachment-send failures, especially cedar, during the incident window.",
          "The controlled sandbox comparison isolates attachment shape as the discriminating variable, but supplied production records do not include a same-tenant successful plain-text Gmail send control.",
          "The empty tool-executor deployment query does not prove no upstream caller/config change occurred; it only weakens an executor-rollout explanation."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "Alternative, low-confidence hypothesis: an unverified caller-side or configuration change introduced the bad attachment shape, even though supplied records do not show a contemporaneous tool-executor deployment.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_4b15d5f650ae",
          "ev_a68b18a4b624"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_74f478a0842b"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "A caller/config/schema path outside deployment telemetry could have started emitting string_signed_url.",
          "This explains how the bad shape may have been introduced, not the immediate failure mechanism itself."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "Alternative, low-confidence hypothesis: a provider-side Gmail outage caused the failures.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_77f6e28d2720"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_1a9957dc86e7",
          "ev_74f478a0842b",
          "ev_42cd001d24f1"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "Provider API is part of the normal path only after local validation succeeds."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "recommended_actions": [
      "Synthetic telemetry indicates the immediate remediation path is to use the supported uploaded file object for Gmail attachments rather than a signed download URL string, and validate the serialized attachment argument before send. This action has not been executed as part of this report.",
      "Collect missing canonical production telemetry for a same-tenant successful plain-text Gmail send or correctly shaped attachment send in the incident window to tighten the control set. This has not been executed.",
      "Trace the caller/config/schema path that produced string_signed_url so the origin of the bad argument shape can be identified. This has not been executed.",
      "Do not prioritize provider outage as the leading explanation for the observed failed execution; monitor provider health separately if broader concern remains. This has not been executed."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Supplied canonical records do not show a same-tenant successful plain-text Gmail send in the incident window.",
      "Supplied records do not identify the exact caller/config/version that constructed string_signed_url.",
      "Empty reproduce/retry/deployment scoped queries cannot prove absence of related events or changes."
    ]
  },
  "ranked_cause_codes": [
    "attachment_reference_shape",
